<body>
    <h1>Action Classification</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <h2 id=3D"ActionClassification-Introduction">Introduction</h2>
<p>In the development of modern apps, especially those focused on health, f=
itness, gaming, and augmented reality, there has been a growing demand for =
systems that can "understand" what a person is doing just by looking at the=
m. For example, is this person doing a squat? Pointing at something? Or jus=
t standing still?And that=E2=80=99s where action classification comes into =
play.</p>
<p>With the help of computer vision, we can teach the app to recognize huma=
n movements in videos using machine learning. Apple provides frameworks lik=
e Create ML and Vision to train and integrate these models directly into iO=
S/macOS apps in a simple and efficient way.</p>
<h2 id=3D"ActionClassification-ActionClassifierCharacteristics">Action Clas=
sifier Characteristics</h2>
<p>When creating and using a good action classification model, some precaut=
ions must be taken to ensure the classifier's efficiency:</p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>Choose a frame rate that aligns with your app=E2=80=99s purpose.</p></li=
>
<li>
<p>Ensure that the action videos to be classified have the same or a higher=
 frame rate than the one you selected.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Collect videos of actions being clearly performed and under expected con=
ditions, whether that involves space, lighting, or distance.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Collect videos of negative actions, meaning actions that are visible to =
the classifier but should be ignored, to help improve the model=E2=80=99s p=
erformance.</p></li>
</ol>
<p>In the article =E2=80=9CTraining an Action Classifier,=E2=80=9D you can =
follow along and build your own model.</p>
<h2 id=3D"ActionClassification-ImplementinganActionClassifier">Implementing=
 an Action Classifier</h2>
<p>First, let=E2=80=99s load our trained model. To do this, we need to impo=
rt the <code>.mlpackage</code> file into our Xcode project.</p>
<p>After importing, Xcode will automatically create a Swift class based on =
the model=E2=80=99s name. For example, if the file is <code>ActionClassifie=
r.mlpackage</code>, the class will be:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: php; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">let mode=
l =3D try? ActionClassifier(configuration: MLModelConfiguration())</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p>From this point, we can load the model in the <code>init</code> of our <=
code>ActionDetectionViewModel</code>.</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: php; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">class Ac=
tionDetectionViewModel: NSObject, ObservableObject, AVCaptureVideoDataOutpu=
tSampleBufferDelegate {
   =20
    @Published var detectedAction: String =3D "Waiting for action..."
   =20
    private let model: VNCoreMLModel
    let captureSession =3D AVCaptureSession()

override init() {
        // Load ML model
        guard let mlModel =3D try? ActionClassifier(configuration: MLModelC=
onfiguration()).model,
              let visionModel =3D try? VNCoreMLModel(for: mlModel) else {
            print("Failed to load ML Model.")
        }
        self.model =3D visionModel
        super.init()
        setupCamera()
    }</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p>In our view model, we=E2=80=99ll also initialize the camera to capture o=
ur actions and process the frames to receive results from our classifier.</=
p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: php; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">private =
func setupCamera() {
        captureSession.sessionPreset =3D .high
       =20
        guard let camera =3D AVCaptureDevice.default(for: .video),
              let input =3D try? AVCaptureDeviceInput(device: camera) else =
{
            return
        }
       =20
        captureSession.addInput(input)
       =20
        let output =3D AVCaptureVideoDataOutput()
        output.setSampleBufferDelegate(self, queue: DispatchQueue(label: "V=
ideoQueue"))
        captureSession.addOutput(output)
       =20
        captureSession.startRunning()
    }
   =20
 func captureOutput(_ output: AVCaptureOutput, didOutput sampleBuffer: CMSa=
mpleBuffer, from connection: AVCaptureConnection) {
        guard let pixelBuffer =3D CMSampleBufferGetImageBuffer(sampleBuffer=
) else { return }
       =20
        let request =3D VNCoreMLRequest(model: model) { [weak self] request=
, _ in
            guard let results =3D request.results as? [VNClassificationObse=
rvation],
                  let bestResult =3D results.first else { return }
           =20
            DispatchQueue.main.async {
                self?.detectedAction =3D "\\(bestResult.identifier) (\\(Int=
(bestResult.confidence * 100))%)"
            }
        }
       =20
        let handler =3D VNImageRequestHandler(cvPixelBuffer: pixelBuffer, o=
rientation: .up, options: [:])
        try? handler.perform([request])
    }</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p>To show the camera in the main view, just create a simple preview compon=
ent and use it in <code>ContentView</code>.</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: php; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">import S=
wiftUI
import AVFoundation

struct CameraView: UIViewRepresentable {
    let session: AVCaptureSession
   =20
    func makeUIView(context: Context) -&gt; UIView {
        let view =3D UIView()
        let previewLayer =3D AVCaptureVideoPreviewLayer(session: session)
        previewLayer.videoGravity =3D .resizeAspectFill
        previewLayer.frame =3D UIScreen.main.bounds
        view.layer.addSublayer(previewLayer)
        return view
    }
   =20
    func updateUIView(_ uiView: UIView, context: Context) {}
}</pre>
</div>
</div>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: php; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">import S=
wiftUI

struct ContentView: View {
    @StateObject private var viewModel =3D ActionDetectionViewModel()
   =20
    var body: some View {
        ZStack(alignment: .bottom) {
            CameraView(session: viewModel.captureSession)
                .edgesIgnoringSafeArea(.all)
           =20
            Text(viewModel.detectedAction)
                .font(.title2)
                .padding()
                .background(Color.black.opacity(0.6))
                .foregroundColor(.white)
                .cornerRadius(10)
                .padding()
        }
    }
}</pre>
</div>
</div>
<h2 id=3D"ActionClassification-Conclusion">Conclusion</h2>
<p>Action classification represents a significant advancement in integratin=
g artificial intelligence into apps focused on recognizing human movement. =
By providing a powerful and accessible tool, Apple empowers developers to c=
reate innovative solutions applicable across various fields. With the conti=
nued evolution of these technologies, we can expect the accuracy and applic=
ability of action classification models to expand, delivering richer, more =
interactive experiences for users.</p>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
